    "source_text": "H2O2  (30%  in  H2O;  0.31  mL,  3.0  mmol)  was  added  dropwise  over 1-2 min to a stirred solution of lepidine 1a (132 μL, 1.0 mmol), concentrated H2SO4 (107 μL, 2.0 mmol),  3-iodooxetane  (368  mg,  2.0  mmol)  and  iron(II)  sulfate  heptahydrate  (80  mg,  0.3  mmol)  in  DMSO (10 mL) at room temperature. After 1-2 min a further portion of iron(II) sulfate heptahydrate (80 mg,  0.3  mmol)  was  added  and  the  mixture  was  stirred  at  room  temperature  for  30  min.  Further  H2O2(0.31  mL,  3.0  mmol)  and  iron(II)  sulfate  heptahydrate  (80  mg,  0.3  mmol)  was  added,  and  the  mixture  was  stirred  for  15  min,  then  poured  into  a  0.2  M  solution  of  NaOH  (30  mL)  and  Et2O  (50  mL).  The  aqueous and organic layers were partitioned and the aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (2 x 25 mL). The  combined  organic  extracts  were  washed  with  brine  (1  x  30  mL),  dried  (MgSO4),  filtered  and  the  solvent  removed  under  vacuum  to  leave  a  crude  oil.  The  oil  was  purified  by  preparative  thin-layer  chromatography  using  EtOAc  /  hexanes  (3:7)  as  eluent  to  give  a  mixture  of  lepidine  1a  and  desired  product 2a  (25  mg),  and  the  desired  product  2a  (82  mg,  40%)  as  a  solid.  An  analytical  portion  of  the  product 2a was recrystallized from EtOAc / hexanes for data purposes",
    "text_sha256": "69eeffdf01229d55c5a289069b9403ac7d15b3f4c49b68b08ca270a283c42da6",
